-- title:
--   Explicit inverse of the Gaussian Toeplitz matrix via q-LU
-- statement:
--   Under the hypotheses of the q-LU factorization ($K$ a field, $z \ne 0$, $q = x^2$, $(q;q)_i \ne 0$ for $i < n$), with $a^{+}_h = (-xz)^h/(q;q)_h$ and $a^{-}_h = (-x z^{-1})^h/(q;q)_h$,
--
--   $$T^{-1} = \Gamma^{-1}\, U(a^{+})\, \Gamma\, L(a^{-})\, \Gamma^{-1},$$
--
--   where $T$ is the Gaussian Toeplitz matrix, $\Gamma$ the diagonal q-Pochhammer matrix and $L, U$ triangular Toeplitz matrices.
--
--   In Lean:
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6QLU.qLU_inv (x z : K) (n : ℕ) (hz : z ≠ 0) (hq : ∀ i < n, qpoch (x ^ 2) i ≠ 0) :
--       (gaussToep x z n)⁻¹ =
--         GamInv (x ^ 2) n * upT (aP x z) * Gam (x ^ 2) n * lowT (aP x z⁻¹) * GamInv (x ^ 2) n
--   ```
